            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0412" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Patch, Isaac: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-09T18:00:00+09:00">August 9, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 9—7:13 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1468. Embassy’s immediately following telegram contains text of a proposed
                    statement to the [<hi rendition="#italic">be</hi>] issued in Shanghai by Vice
                    Consul Isaac Patch from Dairen prior to his departure for the US August 11.
                    Embassy believes this statement would serve useful purpose in China and [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">by?</hi>] illustrating Soviet role in Dairen and
                    position of Chinese as well as restrictions imposed on American
                    representatives.</p>
                <p>Since Patch leaves Shanghai morning of August 11, Dept’s approval of his
                    statement requested. Sent Dept, repeated Shanghai 711.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
